    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working. Both files are now created:\n\n\u2705 **Fixed the bug** in the frai CLI's gate command handler.\n\n**The problem:** The frai CLI was using Commander.js's variadic `[args...]` parameter, which only captures positional arguments (like `init`), not options/flags (like `--ci`). When delegating to the frai-gate CLI, only the positional arguments were being passed through.\n\n**The solution:** Use `process.argv.slice()` directly to capture all arguments after 'gate', which includes both positional arguments and flags. This is a common pattern when delegating to another CLI tool.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Updated `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` gate command handler to use `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)` instead of just `args`\n- Rebuilt the frai package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Verified the fix: running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
